  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_005 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scVI_n200, avgpool) at 0.650 accuracy, and the critical open question is whether the aggregation strategy is optimal. The multimodal multiprofile config (config_030) underperformed the RNA-only multiprofile baseline, suggesting that how profiles are aggregated may interact with downstream fusion. Config_006 is a single-variable change from the best configuration (avgpool → transformer aggregation), directly testing whether a learned, attention-based aggregation captures inter-profile relationships that simple averaging discards. If transformer aggregation outperforms avgpool, it establishes a superior aggregation strategy to carry into multimodal experiments and potentially resolves the config_030 underperformance. If it does not, it confirms avgpool as the right aggregation and redirects effort toward fusion or encoder choices. This is the highest-information single experiment available: it isolates one design axis, builds on the current best result, and its outcome constrains the design of all subsequent multimodal multiprofile experiments."
}

